{
  "format": "texloom",
  "version": 1,
  "metadata": {
    "title": "Smart Irrigation Controller for Small Farms",
    "university": "Example University",
    "department": "Department of Electrical Engineering",
    "course": "EE 491 – Senior Design Project",
    "team": [
      "Sara Ahmed",
      "Omar Khalid",
      "Lina Haddad",
      "Yousef Nasser"
    ],
    "advisor": "Dr. Maria Lopez",
    "date": "December 2026",
    "abstract": "This report presents a low-cost soil-moisture-driven irrigation controller for small farms. The system combines capacitive moisture probes, a water-balance model and long-range radio to water only when needed.\n\nIn a four-week field trial the prototype cut water use by 34% compared with a fixed timer, at a cost of under $60 per zone.",
    "acknowledgements": "We thank our advisor for her guidance, and the university farm for hosting the field trial."
  },
  "doc": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 1
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Introduction"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Small farms waste a large share of their water because irrigation runs on fixed timers that ignore soil conditions and weather. This project designs a low-cost controller that waters only when the soil needs it."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Problem Statement"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Commercial smart controllers cost more than most small farms can justify, and they depend on cloud services that rural areas cannot reach reliably."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Objectives"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "attrs": {
          "start": 1
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Measure soil moisture at three depths every 10 minutes."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Cut water use by at least 30% compared with a timer schedule."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Keep the bill of materials under $60 per zone."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 1
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Background"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Soil moisture sensing falls into two families: "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "resistive",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "italic"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " probes, which are cheap but corrode, and "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "capacitive",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "italic"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " probes, which last longer and are the choice for this design."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Related Work"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Earlier student projects used Wi-Fi modules that drew too much power for solar operation. We use LoRa radios instead, trading bandwidth for range and battery life."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 1
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "System Design"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Figure 3.1 shows the main parts of the system and how they connect."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "figure",
        "attrs": {
          "src": "figures/system-diagram.png",
          "widthPercent": 85
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "caption",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "System block diagram: probes report to the controller, which drives the valve."
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Water Balance Model"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The controller estimates the soil water deficit each hour from evapotranspiration and rainfall:"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "equation",
        "attrs": {
          "latex": "D_t = D_{t-1} + ET_c - P_{\\mathrm{eff}} - I_t"
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Irrigation starts when the deficit exceeds the management allowed depletion, computed from the root-zone depth "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Z_r",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "code"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " and the available water capacity:"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "equation",
        "attrs": {
          "latex": "\\mathrm{MAD} = p \\cdot \\theta_{AW} \\cdot Z_r"
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Sensor Calibration"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Each probe was calibrated against oven-dried samples; the fitted curve has an R² of 0.97."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Hardware"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "bulletList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Microcontroller: low-power ARM Cortex-M0+"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Radio: LoRa transceiver, 868 MHz"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Power: 6 W solar panel with a 3.7 V Li-ion cell"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Actuator: 12 V latching solenoid valve"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Table 3.1 lists the parts and their cost for one zone."
          }
        ]
      },
